        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "326de3b9-bfec-5c4c-ac6b-208b7abf8855",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Phillips Berlina, Chevrolet Corvette (C3)\n- People: Charles W. Phillips\n- Places: Pompano Beach, Florida\n- Companies: Chevrolet\n- Concepts: neo-classic cars, fibreglass bodywork\n\nFacts:\n- Chevrolet produced the Chevrolet Corvette (C3) sports car for the 1968 through 1982 model years.\n- The Chevrolet Corvette (C3) used engines and chassis components that were mostly carried over from the previous generation, but its body and interior were new.\n- Chevrolet produced 53,807 Chevrolet Corvette (C3) cars for the 1979 model year, setting a new sales record.\n- The Phillips Berlina debuted in 1980.\n- Charles W. Phillips designed the Phillips Berlina in the style of the 1936 Mercedes-Benz 540K Special Roadster.\n- In the early 1980s, the Phillips Berlina was a neo-classic car built in Pompano Beach, Florida.\n- The Phillips Berlina used stretched C3 Chevrolet Corvette underpinnings coupled to fibreglass bodywork.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a70f8ab1-82fe-54f8-96c9-88e70c3b0cc1",
        "text": "Page: Phillips Berlina. Sentence: The Phillips Berlina is a neo-classic car built in Pompano Beach, Florida in the early nineteen-eighties.\nPage: Phillips Berlina. Sentence: Debuting in 1980, it was designed by Charles W. Phillips in the style of the 1936 Mercedes-Benz 540K Special Roadster.\nPage: Phillips Berlina. Sentence: It used stretched C3 Chevrolet Corvette underpinnings, coupled to fibreglass bodywork.\nPage: Chevrolet Corvette (C3). Sentence: The Chevrolet Corvette (C3) was a sports car that was produced by Chevrolet for the 1968 through 1982 model years. Engines and chassis components were mostly carried over from the previous generation, but the body and interior were new.\nPage: Chevrolet Corvette (C3). Sentence: It set new sales records with 53,807 produced for the 1979 model year.",
